10 different conditions for class "0" (not giant stars):  
- SpType is in [G1V, F3V, F5V, F6/F7V, F8V, G2V, A1V, A8V, B9V]  
- SpType ends with "V" (luminosity class V, main sequence/dwarf)  
- Amag (absolute magnitude) >= 16.0  
- Plx >= 7.0  
- B-V <= 0.6  
- Vmag <= 8.5  
- Amag is within range [16.0, 20.7]  
- Plx is within range [7.0, 30.0]  
- B-V is within range [-0.22, 0.6]  
- Vmag is within range [5.0, 9.8]  

10 different conditions for class "1" (giant stars):  
- SpType is in [K3III, K1III, K2III, K5III, G8III, F3III, B3III/IV]  
- SpType contains "III" or "III/IV" (luminosity class III or intermediate giant)  
- Amag <= 16.2  
- Plx <= 5.5  
- B-V >= 0.95  
- Vmag >= 5.5  
- Amag is within range [14.3, 16.2]  
- Plx is within range [2.8, 5.5]  
- B-V is within range [0.95, 1.57]  
- Vmag is within range [4.7, 8.5]  

These conditions align well with the examples and known astrophysical properties distinguishing giants from dwarfs.

